# 1.3.5.3 Ordered Lists

An ordered list requires items to appear in a specific sequence, where item n must precede item n+1. Each item begins with a Western-Arabic numeral followed by a close parenthesis. When a list item is further subdivided into a nested unordered list, the nested items must be indented and each starts with an uppercase letter followed by a close parenthesis.  

**Example**:  
1) remove the contents from the box;  
2) assemble the item;  
   A) use a screwdriver to tighten the screws; and  
   B) use a wrench to tighten the bolts;  
3) take a break.
